---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, pageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'Our Place' }];
---

<Layout
  title="About Common Ground Therapy | Richmond, Virginia"
  description="Learn about Common Ground Therapy, a fictional counseling practice for adults in Richmond, Virginia."
  schema={pageSchema([breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, Astro.url.pathname)])}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Our place"
    title="A therapy room with space for the unfinished version of things."
    intro="Common Ground Therapy is Avery Morgan’s fictional Richmond practice for adults who want counseling that feels conversational, curious, and connected to ordinary life."
    crumbs={crumbs}
  />

  <section class="manifesto">
    <div class="container manifesto-grid">
      <div class="manifesto-number">01</div>

      <div class="manifesto-copy">
        <p class="hand-label">The idea behind Common Ground</p>
        <blockquote>
          You do not have to make your life sound neat before it is worth talking about.
        </blockquote>
      </div>

      <div class="manifesto-note">
        <p>
          People rarely arrive with one clean problem and a perfectly organized
          explanation. There may be a conflict, a loss, a reaction that keeps
          surprising you, or several things happening at once.
        </p>
        <p>
          Common Ground is built around meeting that reality directly. The first
          useful question can be as simple as, “What keeps taking up the most
          room lately?”
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="principles-heading">
        <p class="hand-label light">What the room is for</p>
        <h2>Three things that matter here.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-collage">
        <article class="principle principle-one">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Say the real thing</h3>
          <p>
            Therapy can hold uncertainty, contradiction, humor, frustration,
            awkwardness, and the sentence you are not sure how to finish yet.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle principle-two">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Stay curious</h3>
          <p>
            A reaction that seems frustrating may have a history, a purpose, or
            something it is trying to protect. Understanding it can create more
            options than arguing with it.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="principle principle-three">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Keep real life in view</h3>
          <p>
            Work, family, relationships, identity, money, health, culture, and
            the rest of your actual week belong in the conversation when they
            shape what is happening.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="starting-point">
    <div class="container starting-grid">
      <div class="starting-statement">
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>You can enter through whatever door makes sense first.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="starting-note">
        <div class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
          Some people start by reading about anxiety, grief, trauma, or
          relationship concerns. Others are more interested in how Avery works
          and what the different therapy approaches actually mean.
        </p>
        <p>
          Neither route commits you to a label or a method. They are simply
          ways to get a feel for the practice before deciding whether to reach
          out.
        </p>

        <div class="starting-links">
          <a href="/services/">What we help with ↗</a>
          <a href="/approaches/">How we work ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="counselor-band">
    <div class="container counselor-grid">
      <div class="counselor-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="shape plum"></span>
        <span class="shape coral"></span>
        <span class="shape gold"></span>
        <span class="head"></span>
        <span class="body"></span>
        <span class="note">Bring the whole story.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="counselor-copy">
        <p class="hand-label light">Meet the person in the room</p>
        <h2>Avery Morgan, LPC.</h2>
        <p>
          Avery’s fictional profile shows the tone of Common Ground more
          clearly: engaged, conversational, willing to ask a direct question,
          and not especially interested in making therapy sound mysterious.
        </p>
        <a class="profile-link" href="/about/avery-morgan/">
          Meet Avery →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style is:inline>
  .manifesto,
  .principles,
  .starting-point,
  .counselor-band {
    padding:clamp(4.5rem,8vw,7rem) 0;
  }

  .hand-label {
    margin:0 0 .7rem;
    color:#d85f40;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:1rem;
    font-style:italic;
    font-weight:700;
  }

  .hand-label.light { color:#ffd7bf; }

  .manifesto { background:#fffdf8; }

  .manifesto-grid {
    display:grid;
    gap:2rem;
    align-items:start;
  }

  .manifesto-number {
    color:#d85f40;
    font-size:.76rem;
    font-weight:900;
    letter-spacing:.1em;
  }

  .manifesto blockquote {
    max-width:13ch;
    margin:0;
    color:#512c45;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:clamp(2.7rem,5vw,5rem);
    font-weight:500;
    line-height:.96;
    letter-spacing:-.05em;
  }

  .manifesto-note {
    max-width:34rem;
    padding:1.7rem;
    border-left:.45rem solid #f4b21a;
    background:#fff0e5;
  }

  .principles {
    overflow:hidden;
    background:#63384f;
  }

  .principles-heading {
    max-width:46rem;
    margin-bottom:2.7rem;
  }

  .principles-heading h2 {
    margin:0;
    color:white;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5vw,5rem);
    font-weight:500;
    line-height:.98;
  }

  .principle-collage {
    display:grid;
    gap:1rem;
  }

  .principle {
    padding:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);
    color:#512c45;
  }

  .principle > span {
    display:block;
    margin-bottom:2rem;
    font-size:.74rem;
    font-weight:900;
    letter-spacing:.1em;
  }

  .principle h3 {
    margin-bottom:.8rem;
    color:#512c45;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:clamp(2rem,3vw,3rem);
    font-weight:500;
  }

  .principle p { max-width:31rem; }
  .principle-one { background:#f2a082; }
  .principle-two { background:#f4c252; }
  .principle-three { background:#b1b99a; }

  .starting-point { background:#fff8ed; }

  .starting-grid {
    display:grid;
    gap:3rem;
    align-items:center;
  }

  .starting-statement {
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;
    gap:1.2rem;
    align-items:start;
  }

  .starting-statement > span {
    padding-top:.5rem;
    color:#d85f40;
    font-size:.72rem;
    font-weight:900;
  }

  .starting-statement h2 {
    max-width:11ch;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:clamp(2.7rem,5vw,4.8rem);
    font-weight:500;
    line-height:.97;
    letter-spacing:-.045em;
  }

  .starting-note {
    position:relative;
    max-width:34rem;
    padding:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,2.8rem);
    background:#f8e5d6;
    box-shadow:0 18px 40px rgba(81,44,69,.08);
    transform:rotate(1.25deg);
  }

  .tape {
    position:absolute;
    width:6.5rem;
    height:1.4rem;
    left:50%;
    top:-.7rem;
    background:rgba(244,194,82,.72);
    transform:translateX(-50%) rotate(-4deg);
  }

  .starting-links {
    display:flex;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    gap:1rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top:1.5rem;
  }

  .starting-links a {
    color:#8a3f39;
    font-weight:850;
    text-decoration:underline;
    text-underline-offset:.25rem;
  }

  .counselor-band {
    background:#d85f40;
    color:#fff3ea;
  }

  .counselor-grid {
    display:grid;
    gap:3rem;
    align-items:center;
  }

  .counselor-visual {
    position:relative;
    min-height:26rem;
  }

  .shape,.head,.body,.note {
    position:absolute;
    display:block;
  }

  .shape.plum {
    width:15rem;
    height:19rem;
    left:12%;
    top:1rem;
    border-radius:8rem 8rem 1.2rem 1.2rem;
    background:#7f4565;
    transform:rotate(-5deg);
  }

  .shape.coral {
    width:13rem;
    height:8rem;
    right:4%;
    bottom:1rem;
    border-radius:5rem 1.2rem 5rem 1.2rem;
    background:#f39b77;
  }

  .shape.gold {
    width:6rem;
    height:6rem;
    right:10%;
    top:1.5rem;
    border-radius:50%;
    background:#f4b21a;
  }

  .head {
    width:3.6rem;
    height:3.6rem;
    left:calc(12% + 5.7rem);
    top:5.2rem;
    z-index:2;
    border-radius:50%;
    background:#ffd3b8;
  }

  .body {
    width:9rem;
    height:8rem;
    left:calc(12% + 3rem);
    top:9rem;
    z-index:2;
    border-radius:4.5rem 4.5rem 1rem 1rem;
    background:#fff0e4;
  }

  .note {
    right:3%;
    top:9rem;
    z-index:3;
    max-width:10rem;
    padding:.8rem 1rem;
    background:#fff8ed;
    color:#512c45;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:.95rem;
    font-style:italic;
    transform:rotate(4deg);
  }

  .counselor-copy h2 {
    color:white;
    font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;
    font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5vw,4.8rem);
    font-weight:500;
    line-height:.98;
  }

  .counselor-copy p:not(.hand-label) { max-width:35rem; }

  .profile-link {
    display:inline-block;
    margin-top:1rem;
    color:white;
    font-weight:850;
    text-decoration:underline;
    text-underline-offset:.25rem;
  }

  @media(min-width:48rem) {
    .manifesto-grid {
      grid-template-columns:.13fr 1.17fr .7fr;
      gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,5rem);
    }

    .principle-collage {
      grid-template-columns:repeat(12,1fr);
      align-items:start;
      min-height:28rem;
    }

    .principle-one { grid-column:1 / 6; }
    .principle-two { grid-column:5 / 10; margin-top:5rem; }
    .principle-three { grid-column:9 / 13; margin-top:1.5rem; }

    .starting-grid,
    .counselor-grid {
      grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
      gap:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);
    }
  }
</style>
